// Verification half of the investigations-plane record_integrity lane:
// read every stored record back (the whole investigations.records store
// — the unwindowed walk, per its current definition; a chain head
// referencing a predecessor the walk never saw is a deletion),
// recompute each attestation's fingerprint over the canonical
// serialization, and walk the per-case prev_event chains; a Detection
// Finding (2004) drops for every break (fingerprint mismatch = content
// tampered post-stamp, chain-head-missing / link-mismatch = deletion or
// splice). The stored records come back through the catch-all
// reconstruction: ClickHouse has re-sorted the JSON keys, and the
// operator's sort()-canonicalized serialization is what makes the
// recompute match what attest stamped.
//
// SCHEDULED, hourly — the every wrapper, the loader-pipeline shape
// (the core node's opencti-osint-loader / fleet-assets-loader): the
// first walk fires at pipeline start (the previous startup-once
// behavior, preserved) and every 1h re-walks the store. every waits
// for a running walk before starting the next (no concurrent walks);
// restart-on-error still relaunches the pipeline on a hard failure. The
// walk cost grows with the TTL-free case store — the documented
// trade of the unwindowed definition; the cadence is the operator's
// dial if that ever matters.
//
// TWO legs out per break (docs/issues/
// tenzir-record-integrity-attestations.md, the scheduled-walk box):
// - stdout: the raw finding as the operator mints it — pod-log
//   visibility, unchanged.
// - ocsf.Detection_Finding: the finding rides ocsf_derive + ocsf_cast
//   into the lake's class shape and INSERTs with the tenzir user
//   (INSERT/SELECT on ocsf.* — the OnePasswordItem-rendered
//   clickhouse-secrets, the same credential the core node's archive
//   legs read; this node's HelmRelease wires it as
//   TENZIR_SECRETS__CLICKHOUSE_PASSWORD). The written rows land in the
//   table the Grafana tenzir-findings rule reads
//   (03-services/observability/grafana/alerting/tenzir-findings.yaml):
//   class_uid 2004 + severity 4 sit inside the rule's WHERE clauses,
//   so case-store tamper evidence pages through the agent_invoke
//   bridge (homelab-agent -> the investigator) instead of waiting for
//   a human to read pod logs. Tamper evidence is append-only: while a
//   break persists, each hourly walk re-emits its finding and the rule
//   re-fires — re-paging until the tamper is remediated. The written
//   findings carry no attestation (the chains cover
//   investigations.records; the findings live in the ocsf lake) and no
//   row of the walked store is ever written here — the read is the
//   SELECT-scoped investigations-reader, the write only ever INSERTs
//   into the lake, append-only discipline intact.
every 1h {
  from_clickhouse table="investigations.records",
    host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
    port=9000,
    user="investigations-reader",
    password=secret("investigations-reader-password"),
    tls=false
  homelab::investigations::ocsf::verify
  fork {
    to_stdout { write_json }
  }
  ocsf_derive
  ocsf_cast
  to_clickhouse table="ocsf.Detection_Finding",
    host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
    port=9000,
    user="tenzir",
    password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
    tls=false,
    mode="append",
    max_batch_rows=65536
}
